":"1462: Castile takes Gibraltar.","m":8,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Gibraltar","c":3},{"y":1481,"t":"gain","x":"1481: Granada seizes Zahara.","m":12,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1482,"t":"contest_start","x":"1482: the Granada War begins at Alhama.","m":2,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1482,"t":"loss","x":"1482: Castilian forces take Alhama de Granada; reinforcements on 28 April averted its retaking and Ferdinand took command there on 14 May 1482.","m":2,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1483,"t":"loss","x":"1483: Castile retakes Zahara, which Granada had seized in December 1481 (the ledger above).","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahara_de_la_Sierra","c":3},{"y":1485,"t":"loss","x":"1485: Ronda and Marbella fall.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":2},{"y":1486,"t":"loss","x":"1486: Loja falls after a second siege.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":2},{"y":1487,"t":"loss","x":"1487: Vélez-Málaga capitulates on 27 April.","m":4,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1487,"t":"loss","x":"1487: Málaga falls on 18 August after a siege that began on 7 May; al-Zagal 'lost Málaga in 1487'.","m":8,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1487,"t":"contest_end","x":"1487: the western campaign ends with Málaga on 18 August 1487.","m":8,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1489,"t":"contest_start","x":"1489: Castile besieges Baza.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":2},{"y":1489,"t":"loss","x":"1489: Baza surrenders to Castile after the six-month siege.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":2},{"y":1489,"t":"loss","x":"1489: Almería and Guadix surrender through al-Zagal.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Granada","c":1},{"y":1489,"t":"contest_end","x":"1489: the eastern campaign is treated as ended with the surrenders; bridging judgment, the page gives no end date for it.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":1},{"y":1491,"t":"contest_start","x":"1491: the siege of Granada begins.","m":4,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1492,"t":"loss","x":"1492: Granada surrenders.","m":1,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1492,"t":"contest_end","x":"1492: the Granada War ends with the surrender of 2 January (infobox: February 1482 - 2 January 1492).","m":1,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3},{"y":1492,"t":"dissolve","x":"1492: the Emirate of Granada ends, annexed to Castile.","m":1,"cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Mudéjar revolt of 1264-1266","from":1264,"to":1266,"outcome":"Granada broke the peace 'in either late April or early May 1264' and supported the Muslim revolt in Castile's new lands; the Treaty of Alcalá de Benzaide (undated on the page) left Granada paying an annual tribute of 250,000 maravedíes.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_I_of_Granada"},{"name":"Marinid occupation of the Strait and Málaga","from":1275,"to":1294,"outcome":"The Marinids occupied Algeciras, Tarifa and Ronda (1275) and Málaga (1278-1279); Castile captured Tarifa in October 1292; Abu Ya'qub ceded Algeciras and Ronda to Granada in 1294.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Granada"},{"name":"Siege of Algeciras (1342-1344)","from":1342,"to":1344,"outcome":"Algeciras surrendered to Alfonso XI on 26 March 1344 and was incorporated into the Crown of Castile; ten-year truce with an annual tribute of twelve thousand doubloons from Granada.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Algeciras_(1342%E2%80%931344)"},{"name":"Castilian-Granadan war of 1405-1410","from":1405,"to":1410,"outcome":"Ferdinand of Antequera conquered Antequera in 1410.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_I_of_Aragon"},{"name":"Castilian capture of Gibraltar (1462)","from":1462,"to":1462,"outcome":"A small Castilian force took Gibraltar in August 1462, ending Moorish rule there.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Gibraltar"},{"name":"Granada War","from":1482,"to":1492,"outcome":"Castilian-Aragonese victory: Alhama (1482), Ronda and Marbella (1485), Loja (1486), Vélez-Málaga and Málaga (1487), Baza and the east (1489), the Treaty of Granada (25 November 1491) and the surrender on 2 January 1492.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War"}],"certainty":[{"from":1232,"to":1481,"level":"soft","note":"The Castilian frontier is approximate: no page opened gives a boundary line; the Treaty of Jaén (1246) and the Strait cells (Gibraltar, Algeciras, Tarifa) changed hands repeatedly."},{"from":1482,"to":1492,"level":"soft","note":"The front moves by siege; each conquest is a city and its district, not a line."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Granada","title":"Emirate of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granada_War","title":"Granada War"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_I_of_Granada","title":"Muhammad I of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasrid_dynasty","title":"Nasrid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Algeciras_(1342%E2%80%931344)","title":"Siege of Algeciras (1342-1344)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Gibraltar","title":"History of Gibraltar"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_I_of_Aragon","title":"Ferdinand I of Aragon"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_XI_of_Castile","title":"Alfonso XI of Castile"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_IV_of_Granada","title":"Muhammad IV of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yusuf_I_of_Granada","title":"Yusuf I of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ronda","title":"Ronda"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahara_de_la_Sierra","title":"Zahara de la Sierra"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_XIII_of_Granada","title":"Muhammad XIII of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marinid_Sultanate","title":"Marinid Sultanate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_V_of_Granada","title":"Muhammad V of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_al-Hasan_Ali_ibn_Othman","title":"Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Othman"}]}